Certainly! Here's a JSON schema that adheres to the structure and constraints of an fstab file:

```json
<schema>
{
  "$id": "https://example.com/fstab",
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["/"],
  "properties": {
    "/": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "{device}": {
          "type": "object",
          "patternProperties": {
            "^(/[^/]+)+$": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "device": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "mount_point": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "file_system_type": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "options": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "dump": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "pattern": "^[0-1]$"
                },
                "pass": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "pattern": "^[0-2]$"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "device",
                "mount_point",
                "file_system_type",
                "options",
                "dump",
                "pass"
              ]
            }
          },
          "additionalProperties": false
        }
      },
      "required": ["{device}"],
      "additionalProperties": false
    }
  },
  "patternProperties": {
    "^(/[^/]+)+$": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false
    }
  },
  "additionalProperties": false
}
</schema>
```

This schema defines the root object as an object with a single property "/" that contains an object with multiple properties, each representing a mount point in the fstab file. Each mount point object has the required properties "device", "mount_point", "file_system_type", "options", "dump", and "pass", with the specified types and patterns. The schema also includes constraints to ensure that each mount point object only contains the specified properties and no additional properties.

